			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1415,
				8
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize WindServiceHandlers into discrete sub-modules\n\nDecompose the monolithic `WindServiceHandlers` modules (Extensions, Git, Model, Navigation, Output, Storage, Terminal) into a structured tree of individual files, one per exported handler. This aligns with the project's modular architecture and PascalCase naming convention, replacing large stub files with thin `mod.rs` dispatchers that delegate to specific handler implementations.\n\nKey changes:\n- **Extensions:** Extract `GetInstalled`, `GetAll`, `Get`, and `IsActive` into separate modules. Preserve the critical boot-race polling logic (up to 5s) and manifest skeletonization in `ExtensionsGetInstalled` to prevent UI crashes during trusted-publishers migration.\n- **Git:** Isolate `HandleExec` and `HandleClone` etc. into distinct units while retaining the shared `Shared` module for process registration and PID tracking.\n- **Model/Navigation/Storage/Terminal:** Refactor each into a family of single-purpose modules (e.g., `ModelOpen`, `HistoryGoBack`, `StorageSet`) to improve testability and readability.\n- **Dispatcher Update:** Update `mountain_ipc_invoke` in `mod.rs` to route commands to the new nested module paths (e.g., `Git::HandleExec::HandleExec`).\n- **Telemetry:** Standardize OTLP span names to `land:mountain:ipc:<command>` and inject the `CaptureHandler` instrumentation to track per-invocation duration for the Feature Parity dashboard.\n\nThis restructuring eliminates `dead_code` and `unused_variables` lints while clarifying the IPC surface area for future Wind service migrations.",
			"SHA": "f7f34e5ab2e7ad549f1ea09c3416588942ea7a19"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:17:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1415,
				14
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement Wind service adapter bridge and DTOs\n\nIntroduce a comprehensive adapter layer under `Source/IPC/WindServiceAdapters/` to bridge the Mountain Rust backend with the Wind TypeScript UI service contracts. This module serializes Mountain's sandbox configuration into the `WindDesktopConfiguration` structure expected by Sky during boot, and provides concrete implementations for Wind's core service interfaces (File, Storage, Configuration, Environment) using the `CommonLibrary` trait definitions.\n\nKey additions include:\n- **DTOs:** `MountainSandboxConfiguration`, `WindDesktopConfiguration`, and file-specific structures (`FileToDiff`, `FilesToWait`) to serialize launch parameters and state.\n- **Service Wrappers:** `WindFileService`, `WindStorageService`, `WindConfigurationService`, and `WindEnvironmentService` that inject `CommonLibrary` providers (FileSystemReader/Writer, StorageProvider) to satisfy Wind's async service requirements.\n- **Adapter Logic:** `WindServiceAdapter` which transforms raw JSON sandbox configs into the typed `WindDesktopConfiguration` and instantiates service instances with the current `ApplicationRunTime` context.\n\nThis enables the Wind frontend to operate on native Rust services via the Tauri IPC layer, decoupling UI service logic from the underlying OS implementation.\n\nRefs: Land Element Architecture, IPC Bridge",
			"SHA": "1dd8948da9ad46dd9e6188992b3288afae914b16"
		},
