				1401,
				10
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement TLS certificate management IPC command suite\n\nIntroduce a comprehensive set of Tauri commands under `Source/Binary/Build/TlsCommands/` to expose the `CertificateManager` to the Wind/Sky frontend for local TLS/HTTPS provisioning.\n\nThe implementation adheres to PascalCase naming and the project's modular architecture, adding:\n- **DTOs:** `CertificateGenerationResult` and `CertificateStatus` to structure payload responses including expiry timelines and renewal flags.\n- **Lifecycle:** `tls_initialize` loads or generates the root CA; `tls_generate_cert` issues or retrieves server certificates for specific hostnames.\n- **Monitoring:** `tls_check_cert_status` calculates days until expiry and flags renewal needs based on the configured threshold.\n- **Inspection:** `tls_get_all_certs`, `tls_get_server_cert_info`, and `tls_get_ca_cert` provide diagnostic data for the security panel.\n- **Maintenance:** `tls_renew_certificate` and `tls_delete_cert` (currently aliased to renewal) allow manual certificate rotation.\n\nThese commands gate access via the `CertificateManager` state mutex, enabling secure, asynchronous certificate lifecycle operations from the editor UI.\n\nNote: `tls_delete_cert` currently regenerates the certificate as a placeholder until a dedicated deletion logic is implemented in `CertificateManager`.",
			"SHA": "8e396fbf31d1bb878c5a4609f59a4e823f0f2871"
		}
	],
